Open the Esc menu in scenes that have a MENU object.

The menu is loaded as objects on top of the current scene, and its object
is called MENU. Jack's air gauge in the underwater scenes (JACK/EXTRA.MOV)
and the teleporter screen (LAB07/IOD/TEL.MOV) also have an object called
MENU, so pressing Esc there stopped the game with "Duplicate object name
MENU". Only check the menu's names against the other menu objects.

--- a/resource.cpp
+++ b/resource.cpp
@@ -320,7 +320,10 @@
 				SceneObject *so = &_sceneObjectsTable[_sceneObjectsCount];
 				len = fp->readUint16LE();
 				fp->read(so->name, len);
-				for (int i = 0; i < _sceneObjectsCount; ++i) {
+				// The menu is loaded on top of the scene and only its own
+				// objects matter: underwater scenes have a MENU object too.
+				const bool menu = (_state == kStateMenu1 || _state == kStateMenu2);
+				for (int i = menu ? _menuObjectCount : 0; i < _sceneObjectsCount; ++i) {
 					if (strcmp(_sceneObjectsTable[i].name, so->name) == 0) {
 						error("Duplicate object name %s", so->name);
 					}
